.TH KOBAS 1 2000-1月 "kobas.background" "kobas.background"
.SH NAME
kobas.background \- Load a gene set collection from a GMT file as a GSEA background model.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIkobas.background(\fBgmt\fR as string, 
\fBmin_size\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBmax_size\fR as integer = 2147483647, 
\fBduplicate\fR as string = "error");\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Load a gene set collection from a GMT file as a GSEA background model.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBgmt\fB \fR\- the GMT file path.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmin_size\fB \fR\- 
 the minimum number of members of the gene set, gene sets smaller than this
 value will be removed. Default \fB0\fR means no filtering.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmax_size\fB \fR\- 
 the maximum number of members of the gene set, gene sets larger than this
 value will be removed. Default \fB2147483647\fR means no filtering.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBduplicate\fB \fR\- 
 the strategy for the duplicated gene set id in the GMT file, could be
 \fBerror\fR (default, throw an exception) or \fBkeep\fR (keep the first one).
. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a [Background](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.GSEA.Background) model.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
The \fBsize\fR property of the returned background model is the union size of all
 gene set members, it is NOT the number of genes in the expression matrix. The
 GSEA analysis always uses the number of genes in the ranked list as the
 population size \fBN\fR.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
KOBAS
.SH FILES
.PP
gseakit.dll
.PP
